NAME
    files - graphical file manager

SYNOPSIS
    files

DESCRIPTION
    A click-through directory browser over the in-memory VFS
    (/, /bin, /apps, /dev, /proc, /home, /tmp, ...), in two views
    toggled with v.

    List view: each row shows a coloured type tile, the entry name
    and, for files, the size: yellow tiles for directories, green
    for files, magenta for the parent entry. The selected row is a
    full-width light-blue bar.

    Icon view: a grid of flat 32px icons — a yellow folder for
    directories (magenta for the parent), a white document for
    files, a picture-embossed document for images — with the name
    underneath each and the selection as a light-blue cell highlight.

KEYS
    j/k      move down/up (list view)
    h/l      move left/right between icons (icon view)
    v        toggle between the list and icon views
    Enter    open the selected directory, or a .png/.jpg/.jpeg
             picture in picview (Esc hands the window back here)
    Ctrl+C   copy the selected path to the system clipboard
    Ctrl+V   browse to the path the clipboard holds
    Esc      close the window
    Mouse: click to select, release on the same entry to open.

    Drag-and-drop: press a file entry and drag the pointer away
    (the document cursor follows) and release to drop it:

      on another gfx window      that window gets the file (picview
                                 opens it)
      on an app icon             that app opens the file
      on the bare desktop        the file moves to /root/desktop
      back onto the files window the drag is cancelled

    Esc while dragging cancels it too.
    A GUI app (see man calc for how GUI apps are launched).
